{
  "platform": "macOS arm64 on APFS, Homebrew Git 2.56.0",
  "method": "Each series rotated six triples on fresh populated Homebrew clones using the release CLI with history omitted. Checked exact HEAD, tree, index entries, clean status, preservation of unrelated local Git objects and independent history. Ran git fsck in the first candidate workspace of each series. Operating system caches and load were uncontrolled.",
  "hierarchicalStaging": "Four early readers verify individual donor files and clone them into a new private staging directory on the same volume. The candidate checks staged file stamps and directory contents, transfers top-level entries using exclusive rename, and lets Git install symlinks. The fixture owns scratch cleanup. This is a timing experiment, without production recovery guarantees.",
  "indexStatTrial": "Uses the standard direct checkout path, hashes each installed regular file through an open descriptor, checks its metadata again, and fills Git v4 index stat fields for matching files. Git still supplies object names and checkout attributes. A separate fixture edits two files immediately after spawn and restores the old mtime on one before first status. All contents survive. The stat trial misses the restored-mtime edit in all four version and format combinations.",
